><LABEL pos="112,116.21449218749999" font="3" color="432D14" direction="1" style="0">LOAD</LABEL><SYMBOL pos="119,114" id="8" show_power="0" can_scale="0" scale_x="1" scale_y="1" part="0" rotate="5"><FIELD pos="-11,-8" value="Fixed resistor · EU" description="Name" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="0.5,-4.25" value="R2" description="Ref" type="0" show="1"/><FIELD pos="-11,-8" value="" description="Package" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-11,-8" value="" description="TC1" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-11,-8" value="" description="TC2" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="0.5,-1.75" value="330" description="Value" type="0" show="1"/></SYMBOL><WIRE a="118,106" b="118,95"/><LABEL pos="118,95.36625000000001" font="3" color="432D14" direction="1" style="0">SUPPLY</LABEL><WIRE a="118,114" b="118,122"/><LABEL pos="118,114.21449218749999" font="3" color="432D14" direction="1" style="0">LOAD</LABEL><NOTE_TEXT a="7,4" b="233,16.6" font="4" color="432D14" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="0">GY18 · System connections and test plan</NOTE_TEXT><NOTE_TEXT a="147,21" b="233,148" font="1" color="432D14" style="5" fill="3" direction="3" border_style="0">## Follow the system interfaces

**First-year degree · ages 18+**

A system diagram shows where signals enter, how they are conditioned and where the results are used. Labelled connections describe interfaces; physical and software behaviour need separate evidence.

### Your investigation

Follow each signal from source to destination. Mark the reference, expected voltage range, loading and useful test points. Explain how you would test each stage.

### This activity

Draw supplies, references, sensor connections, driver and receiving equipment, with test points. The full mechanical/process/software system remains outside TinyCAD.

### Getting started

This is a connection-planning drawing. Follow each labelled net, identify the real terminals and add your bench measurements. No simulation is attached.

The transistor is an example output driver. Choose a load and base resistor using the actual sensor voltage and load current.

**Explain:** Use an equation, a truth table or a state sequence to justify your prediction. Include units and discuss the model assumptions.

Check the physical layout with your teacher before construction.</NOTE_TEXT></TinyCAD><DSNSETTINGS><SHOW_RULERS>1</SHOW_RULERS></DSNSETTINGS><NETLIST_TYPES><TYPE name="default"/></NETLIST_TYPES></TinyCADSheets>